Dynamic Programmin
Dynamic Programming is an optimization technique used to solve problems by breaking them down into simpler subproblems and storing the solutions to subproblems to avoid redundant computations. It has two approaches - Top-Down Approach (Memoization) and Bottom-Up Approach (Tabulation).